  "summary": "FOIA records analyzed by the Evanston RoundTable show that Evanston PD shares its Flock ALPR network with at least seven out-of-state agencies that searched Illinois ALPR data (in Mount Prospect and Danville) for immigration/ICE-related reasons in 2025. Illinois' Secretary of State has ordered a statewide audit, and Flock has revoked access for 47 out-of-state agencies. Evanston PD has not confirmed whether its data was accessed in these searches and denied a related records request.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Evanston Police Department shared its network of 18 automatic license plate readers with at least seven out-of-state agencies that sent vehicle searches to other Illinois cities for immigration enforcement cases",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock stated that by May 30 it had revoked Illinois network access to 17 out-of-state agencies based on an internal audit, and later revoked access for another 29 at Giannoulias' request",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "the city denied that records request on June 4, citing 'ongoing investigations.'",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
